From: kuloPo <admin@kulopo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Reserve and protect randomized 2-4 GiB JIT space on x86-64 (DigitalisX64 android17 e680eae6), behind berberis.code_window

Upstream (DigitalisX64 platform_frameworks_libs_binary_translation android17, e680eae6, kuloPo, 2026-11-01; Apache-2.0): reserve the
free 2-4 GiB address ranges before arm64 guest execution and allocate the code pools there with lock-free cursors; refuse guest
mmap(MAP_FIXED)/munmap/mprotect/mremap over them (EEXIST/ENOMEM kept for retries), so a guest cannot unmap or overwrite translated code.
The only commit of android17 after our REVISION abefbe2b.
apklayer patch (0063): taken whole (tests included); one conflict with 0044 in MmapForGuest (both kept, the refusal first); and
EnableCodeWindow() runs only with berberis.code_window=on (env BERBERIS_CODE_WINDOW): the reservation is a ~2 GiB PROT_NONE line in the
guest's /proc/self/maps that no device has, and ACE reads the maps. Off (default) nothing changes. Applies after 0062. Module libberberis_arm64.

